WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:06.670
Even by the standards of other famous violent
anomalies, SCP-106, better known as The Old

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.530
Man, is a complete monster.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:15.429
Consider this - SCP-096, the Shy Guy, is a
mindless beast that kills out of pure instinct

00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:17.640
when people see its face.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:23.370
SCP-049, the Plague Doctor, kills by accident
with his deadly touch while trying to help.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:29.029
Even SCP-682 seems to kill because the burning
hatred for all life that resides inside it

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:31.289
is impossible to suppress.

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:37.300
But SCP-106 doesn’t kill out of hatred,
he kills out of love - and what he loves more

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:43.190
than anything else is inflicting pain, misery,
and terror, just for the fun of it.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:48.510
In case you haven’t seen our video on the
subject, SCP-106 is an invincible, sadistic

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:53.680
old man whose anomalous abilities allow him
to walk through solid surfaces.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:58.079
As a result, he’s incredibly hard to contain
- making him one of the scarier Keter-class

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:03.360
anomalies in SCP Foundation containment - and
it’s almost impossible to escape if you

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:04.960
end up on his hit list.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:10.159
But his scariest ability of all is dragging
people into his pocket dimension: A private

00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:15.729
hell where he controls both space and time,
and can do awful things to his captured victims

00:01:15.729 --> 00:01:18.420
to his heart’s content.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:22.740
SCP-106 is downright evil, and he couldn’t
be happier about it.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:26.600
You might assume that there are no hidden
depths to be plumbed when it comes to the

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:32.009
straightforwardly violent monster, but certain
SCP Foundation discoveries about the infamous

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:34.070
Old Man may surprise you.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.810
Meet SCP-978: The Desire Camera.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:42.840
This anomalous Polaroid Camera has the remarkable
ability to reveal the deepest desire of its

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:48.109
subject, and the Foundation tested the camera
on several employees and anomalies - including

00:01:48.109 --> 00:01:49.479
SCP-106.

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:56.509
Now, you might have expected SCP-106’s greatest
desire to be causing more pain, his favorite

00:01:56.509 --> 00:02:01.310
activity, but the researchers were shocked
to find out that wasn’t the case at all.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:07.630
The actual result, according to test logs,
was, quote, “SCP-106 roaming a wheat field.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:12.290
Appears to be approaching an old farmhouse,
while a woman, appearing to be in her mid-sixties,

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:13.540
welcomes 106.”

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:19.709
It turned out that even a creature of pure
malice like SCP-106 may have some hidden secrets

00:02:19.709 --> 00:02:23.700
after all, a prospect that greatly intrigued
Foundation researchers.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.220
While an obscene amount of work had gone into
containing The Old Man and subverting his

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:32.780
powerful anomalous abilities, comparatively
little work had gone into his origins.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.370
And when the Foundation actually started digging,
they were surprised to find that the rabbit

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:40.900
hole was far, far deeper than they’d ever
imagined.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:46.150
Much like the Joker, The Old Man’s origin
story is multiple choice.

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:51.159
Out of the reams of research into SCP-106’s
origin, we’ve narrowed it down to the three

00:02:51.159 --> 00:02:56.019
most plausible possibilities for how a creature
like The Old Man could come to exist: The

00:02:56.019 --> 00:03:00.519
Divergent Species Theory, the Scranton Theory,
and the Corporal Lawrence Theory.

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:03.060
And today we’re going to explore all of
them.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.319
First, let’s look at the Divergent Species
Theory.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:10.769
The main basis for this theory is information
gleaned from a tale known as “Once But Not

00:03:10.769 --> 00:03:11.769
Now.”

00:03:11.769 --> 00:03:16.489
This tale is seen as a collection of memories
from the atrophied mind of The Old Man, detailing

00:03:16.489 --> 00:03:18.799
his origins thousands of years prior.

00:03:18.799 --> 00:03:23.390
It’s worth remembering that a lot of these
memories are, of course, highly subjective

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:24.819
and interpretive.

00:03:24.819 --> 00:03:29.110
If they are to be taken as the authentic memories
of the Old Man, then it is also important

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:35.739
to note that - as a deranged, compulsive sadist
- details of his memories are possibly unreliable.

00:03:35.739 --> 00:03:39.980
That being said, according to the reports
contained within “Once But Not Now”, The

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:44.739
Old Man was once a member of a hominid family
similar to that of humans, but displaying

00:03:44.739 --> 00:03:50.659
the anomalous powers we’ve come to expect
from SCP-106: Enhanced strength, corrosive

00:03:50.659 --> 00:03:54.450
mucus, and the ability to pass through solid
objects.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:58.769
In the documents, it is implied that the primary
source of prey for the Old Man’s species

00:03:58.769 --> 00:04:00.019
was actually neanderthals.

00:04:00.019 --> 00:04:04.470
They had basic tribal cultures that allowed
them to organize hunting parties for the purpose

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.599
of bringing food back to their camps.

00:04:06.599 --> 00:04:11.810
They even had a semblance of socially-enforced
laws - leaving members of their tribe to starve

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:14.810
after they committed murder against their
own species.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:19.430
If things had played out differently, this
species may have stuck around, perhaps even

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:25.199
surpassing humanity and becoming the dominant
species on Earth: An entire thriving culture

00:04:25.199 --> 00:04:26.790
of SCP-106.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:32.350
However, as time passed, the neanderthals
were eventually hounded to extinction.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:37.610
This destroyed the primary food source for
SCP-106’s species, which - if you have even

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:43.099
a basic familiarity with evolutionary biology
- never bodes well for a species.

00:04:43.099 --> 00:04:47.580
As The Old Man’s species turned its attention
to humanity, it found they weren’t nearly

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.330
as easy to prey upon.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:55.210
As a result, their species slowly fell into
decline and eventually slipped into near extinction.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:05:00.180
The Old Man, most likely the last of his kind,
went into a state of hibernation within a

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:01.180
tree.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:04.780
He remained in the tree for what may have
been thousands of years, before eventually

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:10.610
climbing out into a world that had long since
forgotten anything like him had ever existed.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:16.160
The Old Man woke up into a strange new world,
filled with alien structures and garish lights.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.870
He wandered, confused and hungry, haunted
by the knowledge that he was the last one

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:22.440
left of his kind.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:26.720
He wandered around the new world until he
found what he described as “a nest” - likely

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.419
just a normal, human home.

00:05:28.419 --> 00:05:32.979
He became distressed by the structures and
lights around him, until finally happening

00:05:32.979 --> 00:05:36.250
upon a food source that he hungrily ate.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:39.810
This food source turned out to be a human
infant.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:44.150
Not long after that, he was apprehended by
figures described as the “men in white coats”

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:47.570
who are likely to be agents of the SCP Foundation.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:49.949
He was contained not long after that.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:54.610
These days, his only motivating factor is
the search for pain and anguish - the only

00:05:54.610 --> 00:06:00.069
things that can give this very, very old man
any semblance of feelings anymore.

00:06:00.069 --> 00:06:03.570
Of course, this is actually the least popular
of the three theories.

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:09.889
But it does pose a rather disturbing question:
If ever there was a whole species of SCP-106,

00:06:09.889 --> 00:06:13.880
is it really possible that our species would
be able to outlast them?

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:19.440
The second most popular theory was that SCP-106
was not only once human, but an extremely

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.349
important Foundation researcher.

00:06:21.349 --> 00:06:23.379
Namely, Dr. Robert Scranton.

00:06:23.379 --> 00:06:28.129
If that name sounds familiar to you, it may
be because you’ve heard of the famous Scranton

00:06:28.129 --> 00:06:29.710
Reality Anchors.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:33.789
These devices, inspired by Scranton, have
been the Foundation’s greatest tools in

00:06:33.789 --> 00:06:36.639
combating the anomalous effects of reality
warpers.

00:06:36.639 --> 00:06:42.710
And, if the Scranton Theory about the origin
of 106 is to be believed, it’s darkly ironic

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:48.039
that it would be a reality-warping anomaly
that would bring Dr. Scranton to his unfortunate

00:06:48.039 --> 00:06:49.039
end.

00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:54.300
The horrors began on January 2nd, in the year
2000, when Dr. Scranton and his wife, Dr.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:59.229
Anna Lang, were testing a new technology:
the Lang-Scranton Stabilizer.

00:06:59.229 --> 00:07:02.810
This was the technology that would lay the
groundwork for the Reality Anchors that would

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.979
later be created in Scranton’s name.

00:07:04.979 --> 00:07:10.220
However, the stabilizer was ironically anything
but stable, and caused what is known as a

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:13.449
momentary Class-C "Broken Entry" Wormhole.

00:07:13.449 --> 00:07:17.289
Scranton was sucked into the wormhole, and
transported to a pocket dimension known as

00:07:17.289 --> 00:07:21.039
SCP-3001, or “The Red Reality.”

00:07:21.039 --> 00:07:26.850
Many people assumed Scranton was dead, but
the reality was far more horrific.

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:31.690
SCP-3001, which the still-living Scranton
and the control pad of the stabilizer were

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:35.900
sucked into, was a kind of empty, infinitely-extending
void.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:42.150
The laws of reality did not apply in the darkened
void of 3001: There was no space, no light,

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:43.909
no passage of time.

00:07:43.909 --> 00:07:49.180
It was the absence of all existence, except
for Scranton who was the one speck of existence

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:50.849
trapped inside.

00:07:50.849 --> 00:07:55.030
As whatever passed for “time” went on,
Scranton could only speak to a small audio

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:57.469
recorder embedded in the console.

00:07:57.469 --> 00:08:02.920
It became his only company, the one thing
anchoring him to some semblance of sanity.

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.629
But of course, that couldn’t last forever.

00:08:05.629 --> 00:08:10.280
As he came to terms with the reality of his
situation, Dr. Scranton became overtaken by

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:12.780
fear, and then despair.

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:17.669
He started to lose hope that he would ever
exit the pocket dimension of SCP-3001, and

00:08:17.669 --> 00:08:23.229
his coherent speech became terrified, disconnected
ramblings as his mind fell apart.

00:08:23.229 --> 00:08:28.530
He tried to end his life 184 times while trapped
there, but it never worked.

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:33.510
He took the damage of each attempt, slowly
becoming unrecognizable, but there was no

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:37.340
death to grant him escape from SCP-3001.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:42.730
As time went on, the very state of reality
within the Red Reality began to decay.

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:47.240
Matter started to become anti-matter, and
Robert Scranton felt himself coming apart

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:49.980
at the seams and floating into nothingness.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:55.510
He was still conscious and very much aware
as his personality - perhaps even his very

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:58.610
soul - fractured and drifted away with his
body.

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:04.050
In total, he spent almost six years inside
the broken pocket dimension, though this probably

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:06.260
felt like an eternity to him.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:11.170
Eventually, even the console vanished from
the Red Reality and returned back to our own,

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:15.290
leaving whatever was left of Robert Scranton
truly alone.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:19.010
Those who loved him prefer to believe that
he’s now as close to dead as is possible

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:25.010
within SCP-3001, but people who believe in
the Scranton Theory have different ideas…

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:29.450
Dr. Robert Scranton - or rather, whatever
he became - was headstrong.

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:34.490
He wanted to escape the Red Reality at any
cost so he could be reunited with his wife,

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:35.960
Dr. Anna Lang.

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:40.920
Through sheer force of willpower, Dr. Scranton
pulled his disparate matter back together,

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.790
but it didn’t come back in the way it used
to be.

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:45.650
There was something wrong.

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:46.750
Terribly wrong.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:51.910
He was now something less than human: SCP-106.

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:57.760
Scranton, a man who’d spent his life developing
technology to keep reality consistent, was

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:00.420
about to build his own reality.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:04.570
He would build, destroy, and rebuild, again
and again.

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:09.200
He would create a perfect reality for him
and his beloved Anna - which would later become

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.020
his trademark pocket dimension.

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:15.810
But when Anna saw the monster he’d become,
she was horrified by him.

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:20.590
His very touch destroyed her, his corrosive
mucus melting her away.

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:23.490
All that was left was the monster he’d become.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:27.280
The Old Man, SCP-106.

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:31.540
Of course, there’s one more theory about
the origin of SCP-106.

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:36.410
If ever you’ve heard the wall-walking monster
referred to as Uncle Larry, this next story

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:37.410
is why.

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:43.280
In fact, it’s the most widely believed of
all the SCP-106 origin theories: The Corporal

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:44.530
Lawrence Theory.

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:46.760
So, who is Corporal Lawrence?

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:50.880
We actually know very little about the man,
aside from the fact he was a military officer

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.790
during World War One.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:56.200
Our knowledge of him comes from firsthand
accounts of the soldiers serving under him

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.470
in the trenches.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:03.220
The Corporal was described as a plain, aloof,
and vacant man, with a tendency to stare.

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:07.840
Many of the soldiers disliked him on account
of his incredibly flat personality, but perhaps

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:13.330
even more so because Lawrence always seemed
to be followed by the smell of rot.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:17.680
Strange incidents also seemed to follow him
around - like soldiers in his barracks seeing

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:20.690
greater numbers of sicknesses like trench
foot.

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:22.930
It was almost as if he was cursed.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:25.220
And perhaps he was.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:29.310
One fateful day, Lawrence and his men needed
to raid an enemy trench.

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:34.000
They infiltrated the trench, and found that
everyone there was dead, and covered in a

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:36.280
corrosive, black slime.

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:41.350
Worse still, Corporal Lawrence discovered
a strange, black hole in the trench, filled

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:43.030
with the same black substance.

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:49.360
He then collapsed into this hole, before climbing
out, clearly shaken by the experience.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:51.260
After that, everything went downhill.

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:55.950
Corporal Lawrence appeared to completely change
his personality, becoming a perpetually-grinning

00:11:55.950 --> 00:12:01.050
eccentric with a head full of strangely morbid
and sadistic thoughts.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:06.440
At a certain point, his body seemed to reproduce
the same corrosive mucus he fell into, causing

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:10.180
pain and sickness to his fellow soldiers wherever
he went.

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:14.100
In the end, after the horrific deaths of some
of the soldiers working under him, Corporal

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:18.410
Lawrence and his men were apprehended and
interred at a military hospital.

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:22.640
Not long after though, he disappeared, along
with the rest of his men.

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:27.120
The only trace that remained was on the former
Corporal Lawrence’s hospital bed: Traces

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:33.010
of the corrosive, black mucus, and a ring
of human teeth - pulled from the heads of

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:35.480
every single person on the ward.

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:40.260
The next time he was seen, Corporal Lawrence
truly was no more.

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:47.400
Only SCP-106 remained, and in his own sick
little way, he’d never been happier.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:52.070
And there you have it, the three most popular
theories into the origin of SCP-106.

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:55.940
Which, if any, do you think is the most likely
theory?

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:57.640
Or do you have one of your own?

00:12:57.640 --> 00:12:59.680
Let us know down in the comments.

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:02.310
And remember: Keep an eye on the walls.

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:06.260
You never know when the Old Man will drop
in for a visit...

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:12.660
Now check out “SCP-106 - The Old Man Escape”
and “SCP-3001 - Red Reality” for a deeper

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:16.680
exploration into some of the topics and concepts
discussed in this video.

